    "extraction_notes": [
      "The supplied datasheet contains usable plotted curves on p. 3. Curve points were manually digitized from visible plotted lines without interpolation from tabulated values.",
      "The zener characteristics plot includes a 4.3 V nominal family trace for BZT52C4V3S and uses a logarithmic IZ axis with pulsed TA = 25 degC conditions.",
      "The electrical characteristics table gives VZ minimum 4.0 V, nominal 4.3 V, and maximum 4.6 V at IZT = 5 mA; the nominal value is recorded as breakdown_voltage.",
      "The electrical characteristics table gives ZZT maximum 90 ohm at IZT = 5 mA and ZZK maximum 600 ohm at IZK = 1 mA.",
      "The electrical characteristics table gives maximum reverse leakage IR = 3 microA at VR = 1.0 V and maximum admissible zener current IZM = 5 mA.",
      "The datasheet publishes typical capacitance family curves versus nominal zener voltage at 0 V bias, 1 V bias, and bias at 50 percent of nominal VZ, but it does not publish a single capacitance value for BZT52C4V3S at a specified reverse voltage, so specs.capacitance is null.",
      "No reverse-recovery time or switching test is published, so specs.reverse_recovery is null.",
      "The temperature-coefficient table range for BZT52C4V3S is -3.5 to 0 mV/degC at IZTC, and the p. 3 family temperature-coefficient curve is transcribed in V/degC.",
      "The plotted curves are typical family characteristics and should not be treated as guaranteed limits for the individual BZT52C4V3S part."
    ],
